@startuml read-path
title US-01: Read Path - Initial Map Load and Scoped Live Updates

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

actor Operator
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Express API" as API
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "TimescaleDB\nuser_workspaces" as TSDB

== Authenticated Connection and Scope Load ==

Operator -> Dashboard : opens live map
Dashboard -> API : GET /stream?token=<JWT>\nUpgrade: websocket

API -> TSDB : SELECT scope FROM user_workspaces WHERE user_id = $1
TSDB --> API : { geo_region.bounds, entity_types, alert_types }

API --> Dashboard : 101 Switching Protocols

== Initial Map State ==

Dashboard -> API : send { type: "initial_load" } over WebSocket

API -> Redis : SCAN entity:live:* (batched)\nfor each key: HGETALL entity:live:{entity_id}

note over API
  Initial load scans all live entity keys.
  Each result is filtered against the operator's
  saved scope before being included in the response:
  - entity position within geo_region.bounds
  - entity_type in scope.entity_types
  Expired keys are absent automatically (Redis TTL).
end note

Redis --> API : live entity positions (all currently active)

API --> Dashboard : push initial state\n{ entities: [ { entity_id, lat, lon,\n  entity_type, last_seen_ms }, ... ] }\n(scope-filtered subset only)

Dashboard --> Operator : map renders with all\nin-scope entities at current positions

== Live Updates (ongoing) ==

note over API, Redis
  After initial load, ongoing position updates
  arrive via Redis pub/sub from the Position Consumer.
  Each update is scope-filtered before push.
  See US-02 update-push for the per-update flow.
end note

@enduml
